  "lineage": "Afro-Brazilian orisha religion of Recife and neighbouring Northeastern states, called Xangô after the thunder orisha and centred on Nagô houses such as the Sítio de Pai Adão (Ilê Obá Ogunté). Songs for the orishas in a Yoruba-derived liturgical language are led by a soloist and answered by the initiates over a set of ilú drums with an iron bell and a beaded gourd rattle. A generic membrane-drum card stands in for the ilú drums and the source-unspecified agogô for the bell.",
